--##################################################################
--# NOT PORTED: the original's last sector, '  ' (meta table check),
--# lines 1789-1854 of the original file.
--#
--# It opens with  --+SYSTEM server kill; / clean; / server start;  and
--# natc's 'clean' is destroydb + createdb: it wipes the database this
--# suite runs on and rebuilds it without the settings the runner put
--# there. natc-check.sh passes --auto-init=OFF to keep exactly that
--# path away from the isolated instance.
--#
--# The wipe is also load-bearing for the sector itself: what it freezes
--# is an absolute TABLE_ID (105). Without a pristine database that value
--# is a function of how many tables the instance has ever created, so
--# the sector cannot be re-recorded stably in the first place.
--#
--# Substitute for the coverage: disk-catalog-check.sh and
--# NativeGlobalIndexClaude/meta/ read the same catalog rows without
--# printing absolute ids; batch 6 (meta/) revisits the same ground.
--##################################################################
--##################################################################
--+SECTOR 27; FINALIZATION
--##################################################################
